<title>AUSTRIA: CA preferred up on Bank Austria rumours.</title>
<headline>CA preferred up on Bank Austria rumours.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferred shares in Creditanstalt climbed 1.59 percent in a weak market on Wednesday on rumours of a possible bid by Bank Austria for the government's 70 percent stake in the flagship bank.</p>
<p>At 0955 GMT Creditanstalt preferred shares were trading up 8.15 schillings or 1.59 percent at 522.15.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares can only be up in connection with the rumours,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Bank Austria's supervisory board will discuss making an offer for Creditanstalt-Bankverein when it meets at 1500 GMT today, Austrian news agency APA said.</p>
<p>-- Elizabeth Fullerton, Vienna newsroom, +431 53112257</p>
</text>
